     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum recommended dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is twice that limit. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nI suspect a typo. These are some common intended doses:\n- 500 mg three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into smaller doses, such as 850 mg twice daily\n\nPlease tell me the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, please confirm that. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
